<h2>Questions from Scranton property owners</h2><div class="faq"><details><summary>Is mine subsidence covered by my homeowners policy?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Usually not. Most homeowner policies exclude earth movement, including mine subsidence. The Mine Subsidence Insurance program run by the Pennsylvania Department of Environmental Protection offers separate coverage.</p></div></details><details><summary>My double block has one roof and two owners. How does a claim work?<span class="pm" aria-hidden="true"></span></summary><div class="faq-a"><p>Each owner&#x27;s policy typically covers their own share of the building. Coordinating the scope so the repair is done as one job, priced fairly, is often where an independent estimate helps.</p></div></details></div>
